                        "review": "this game has a lot of charm but also has some big shortcomings\n\n1) your character naturally walks so you have to hold shift the whole game in order to run\n\n2) the platforms are pretty slippery if you are on basically any sort of skinny incline\n\n3) the jumping is bad because if you jump from any higher than a regular jump say like off of a cliff or whatnot your character will hit an invisible wall and stop you midair and also if you jump without moving you will have basically no momentum and barely will be able to move in the air which makes jumping feel bad. its a good thing you respawn instantly with no downside on the last area of regular ground because you will die a lot in the jumping sections.\n\n4) one of the puzzles has you collect 4 pieces 2 of which are useless and not needed for the puzzle\n\n5) the last puzzle (timing the pushing pillars) is a piece of crap puzzle I tried for about a 1/2 hour and I gave up between not having a good viewing angle, spells moving as fast as a snail and the cargo having wonky physics It really was not worth it for me\n\n6) the camera is not naturally on your looking around unless you have something picked up then it does it\n\n7) often you can hear the song looping because it doesn't have a smooth transition",
